# Iron · Fe · gate 26

**Iron** (Fe) is element **26** of the periodic table — a **transition metal**, period 4, group 8, d-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **55.845**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
Symbol Fe, from ferrum; the core of the Earth and of your blood; where stellar fusion ends and civilization began.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **26** falls on **0:1 — second valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **1**. That state is *the second reach — the diffuse, the airy, the not-quite-held* — the nature of emergence here is **ethereal**. Iron is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — ethereal
This emergent carries the **ethereal** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#9a7cff`.

